Fv bound to FC27-MSP214–30 and 3D7-MSP214–30 were compared.","assertion_origin":"source","source_url":"https://www.iedb.org/database_export_v3.php","record_url":"http://www.iedb.org/assay/2460983","link_scope":"record","measurements":[],"target_external_id":"http://www.uniprot.org/uniprot/P50498","assay_ids":["2460983"],"receptor_group_id":"691","id":"ix_17049483b27a677ca930","target_id":"target:merozoite-surface-protein-2-f809e02f5ea9","target_name":"Merozoite surface protein 2"},{"antibody_id":"ab_d055250c405025c62998","target_raw":"Merozoite surface protein 2","relationship":"binds","evidence":"CURATED","source":"iedb","source_record_id":"691","reference":"http://www.iedb.org/reference/1028986","epitope":"NAYNMSIRR","assay":"nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) · qualitative binding","note":"The binding of epitope-specific 6D8 scFv to FC27 MSP2 peptide containing the epitope was compared to  the 3D7 MSP2 (14-30) peptide and the epitope MSP2 (14-22) by NMR spectroscopy. Comparisons of the spectrum of 6D8 scFv bound to MSP214–22 with those of 6D8 scFv bound to FC27-MSP2 (14–30) and 3D7-MSP2 (14–30) indicated that the C-terminal extension of the peptide induced significant differences in the spectrum of 6D8, suggesting that MSP2 residues 24 to 30 interact with 6D8 scFv in solution, even though such interactions were not observed crystallographically. Moreover, more subtle differences were observed when the spectra of 6D8 scFv bound to FC27-MSP214–30 and 3D7-MSP214–30 were compared.","assertion_origin":"source","source_url":"https://www.iedb.org/database_export_v3.php","record_url":"http://www.iedb.org/assay/2460984","link_scope":"record","measurements":[],"target_external_id":"http://www.uniprot.org/uniprot/P50498","assay_ids":["2460984"],"receptor_group_id":"691","id":"ix_4982be0ed38eea739467","target_id":"target:merozoite-surface-protein-2-f809e02f5ea9","target_name":"Merozoite surface protein 2"},{"antibody_id":"ab_d055250c405025c62998","target_raw":"Merozoite surfac